Z||000000||pontiacs4me||03-26-2001||05:44 PM||||Ok,<P>I visited my local wrecking yard today to look for some camaro parking lights for my flush mount project, anyway while looking around I came across a 1989 toronado with a 3800 and a 440 transmission.  The yard owner told me that they are both good, and he would sell me the whole works for $600.  I would then go through the engine port the heads, bore it out, balance it port the intake, bigger injectors good exhaust system, etc, etc.  What kind of power will I be looking at?  I want to keep it still sensable with good mileage, but I want this thing to run a new trans am no problem.  Ok, what all will I have to adapt into the computer system?  The car is an 87, the 2.8 thats in it now is a 85 and the 3800 is a 89.  Ok about the 440 transmission, Im going to use it instead of the 125 thats in there now.  what all will I need to mount it up to the cradle?  What about the cv shafts?  Is $600 a good price, I think I might just find a running car I can probably get one for about that price?  What all models of cars had that same setup with the 440 tranny and the 3800?  thanks in advance.||||reg||1
